WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:16.978
"Big Spot's saddle pad is missing?"

2
00:00:17.378 --> 00:00:18.038
Maggie said.

3
00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:19.759
"What do you mean?

4
00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:23.541
I put it back in the tack room, just like always!"

5
00:00:24.681 --> 00:00:25.821
"What's a tack room?"

6
00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:27.462
Cole whispered to Henry.

7
00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:31.724
"I think it's where they keep the horses' equipment," he answered.

8
00:00:32.764 --> 00:00:33.485
"Are you sure?"

9
00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:35.427
Ms. Wood was asking Maggie.

10
00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:38.109
"Because the other pads were there.

11
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.531
But yours wasn't with them."

12
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:43.113
"I'm positive!"

13
00:00:43.574 --> 00:00:44.614
Maggie insisted.

14
00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:48.838
"I remember because it was kind of damp from Spot's sweat.

15
00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:53.342
I could feel it through my shirt when I carried everything back to the tack room."

16
00:00:54.823 --> 00:00:56.425
Ms. Wood didn't look convinced.

17
00:00:56.445 --> 00:01:00.088
"Well, I haven't seen it since your last lesson.

18
00:01:01.052 --> 00:01:05.354
If it doesn't turn up soon, I'll have to speak to your parents about replacing it."

19
00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:08.496
Henry looked at Cole, worried.

20
00:01:09.537 --> 00:01:10.797
Had the thief struck again?

21
00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:14.680
"I put a different pad under Spot's saddle," Ms.

22
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.520
Wood went on.

23
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.121
"You can use that one for today."

24
00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:20.503
The barn owner hurried away.

25
00:01:21.643 --> 00:01:23.965
Maggie stomped toward Big Spot's stall.

26
00:01:24.925 --> 00:01:25.866
The boys followed.

27
00:01:25.886 --> 00:01:28.687
"I can't believe this!"

28
00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:29.868
Maggie cried.

29
00:01:30.912 --> 00:01:33.875
"It's bad enough that my parents might not let me ride anymore.

30
00:01:33.895 --> 00:01:36.577
Now I have to worry about Ms.

31
00:01:36.737 --> 00:01:38.759
Wood kicking me out of the barn too!"

32
00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:42.222
"How much does a saddle pad cost?"

33
00:01:42.582 --> 00:01:43.343
Henry asked.

34
00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:47.126
"Why?" Maggie looked hopeful.

35
00:01:47.146 --> 00:01:49.328
"Are you going to buy Ms.

36
00:01:49.368 --> 00:01:51.630
Wood a new one so she doesn't tell my parents?"

37
00:01:53.271 --> 00:01:58.716
"No. I'm trying to figure out whether the thief could sell that pad for a lot of money."

38
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.781
"Probably not."

39
00:02:01.902 --> 00:02:04.003
Maggie started changing into her riding boots.

40
00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.445
"The pad was kind of old.

41
00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:10.767
And saddle pads only cost about 15 dollars when they're new.

42
00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:15.070
I looked at some when Mom took me to the store to buy my riding clothes."

43
00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:18.973
"This case doesn't make sense," Cole said.

44
00:02:18.993 --> 00:02:22.575
"The thief is stealing really weird stuff."

45
00:02:23.716 --> 00:02:24.477
Henry nodded.

46
00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:29.000
"It's weird that only Maggie's stuff has disappeared.

47
00:02:30.092 --> 00:02:34.595
And it's even weirder that some of the missing stuff is valuable and some isn't."

48
00:02:34.615 --> 00:02:40.638
"A thief could sell Maggie's bracelet or her new riding gloves," Cole said.

49
00:02:40.658 --> 00:02:43.760
"And the check was worth money too, of course.

50
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.561
But why steal one sock?

51
00:02:47.682 --> 00:02:49.463
Or a sweaty old saddle pad?"

52
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:52.525
"Who cares why someone did it?"

53
00:02:52.885 --> 00:02:53.545
Maggie said.

54
00:02:53.565 --> 00:02:56.307
"We just need to figure out who did it.

55
00:02:57.407 --> 00:02:58.388
And fast!"

56
00:02:59.404 --> 00:03:01.265
"Don't worry," Henry told her.

57
00:03:01.285 --> 00:03:03.506
"I have a plan, remember?"

58
00:03:03.526 --> 00:03:07.027
"Good. I hope it works."

59
00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.329
Maggie started getting her pony ready, and the boys wandered off.

60
00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:13.670
"Do you think your plan will work?"

61
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:14.771
Cole asked.

62
00:03:15.831 --> 00:03:18.972
Henry stooped to pat Little Spot as the dog ran up to them.

63
00:03:18.992 --> 00:03:20.673
"I don't know.

64
00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:24.114
But it's the best plan I can think of right now."

65
00:03:25.855 --> 00:03:27.536
He was carrying a plastic bag.

66
00:03:28.596 --> 00:03:31.078
Reaching inside, he pulled out a baseball glove.

67
00:03:31.098 --> 00:03:35.540
"Are you sure you want to risk losing your autographed glove?"

68
00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.661
Cole asked.

69
00:03:36.681 --> 00:03:38.722
"It's really cool.

70
00:03:39.743 --> 00:03:41.724
Plus your parents will be mad if you lose it."

71
00:03:43.285 --> 00:03:45.106
"I won't lose it," Henry said.

72
00:03:45.126 --> 00:03:48.368
"We'll be hiding and watching it, remember?"

73
00:03:49.408 --> 00:03:50.449
That was his plan.

74
00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.352
The baseball glove had been autographed by several famous baseball players.

75
00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.641
Anyone could see it was worth a lot of money.

76
00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:03.683
Henry was planning to put the glove in the barn aisle where everyone would notice it.

77
00:04:04.864 --> 00:04:08.605
Then he and Cole would hide out and see if anyone tried to take it.

78
00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:13.387
With luck, they'd catch the thief before Maggie's riding lesson started!

79
00:04:13.407 --> 00:04:19.850
"If Jill is stealing because she needs money, she'll definitely grab this glove," Cole said.

80
00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:24.012
"If Zach's the thief, he might take it too," Henry said.

81
00:04:25.436 --> 00:04:26.657
"He loves baseball.

82
00:04:27.717 --> 00:04:30.038
And we don't know what Eleanor's motive might be.

83
00:04:31.298 --> 00:04:32.719
Maybe she needs money too.

84
00:04:33.859 --> 00:04:37.481
My aunt and uncle keep saying that riding is an expensive sport."

85
00:04:38.561 --> 00:04:39.802
He set his glove down.

86
00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:43.663
Then he and Cole hid in an empty stall nearby.

87
00:04:45.144 --> 00:04:47.185
It wasn't long before they heard footsteps.

88
00:04:48.385 --> 00:04:51.226
Henry peeked out and saw Zach coming down the aisle.

89
00:04:51.246 --> 00:04:53.607
"Hey, what's that?"

90
00:04:54.068 --> 00:04:54.768
Zach muttered.

91
00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.341
He stopped and picked up the glove.

92
00:04:57.361 --> 00:04:59.583
"Whoa, cool!"

93
00:04:59.903 --> 00:05:00.383
he said.

94
00:05:00.404 --> 00:05:03.265
"Guess someone will come back to look for this."

95
00:05:04.326 --> 00:05:05.987
He dropped the glove where he'd found it.

96
00:05:06.908 --> 00:05:08.109
Then he kept walking.

97
00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:10.690
"Zach didn't take the bait!"

98
00:05:11.051 --> 00:05:11.811
Cole whispered.

99
00:05:11.831 --> 00:05:13.692
"I guess he's innocent."

100
00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:15.494
Henry nodded.

101
00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:20.377
"Shh! Here comes Eleanor."

102
00:05:21.498 --> 00:05:22.979
Eleanor hurried down the aisle.

103
00:05:22.999 --> 00:05:27.621
"Spot? Spot, where are you?"

104
00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:28.541
she called.

105
00:05:30.181 --> 00:05:34.482
She was so busy calling her dog that she almost tripped over the glove before she saw it.

106
00:05:35.563 --> 00:05:37.543
Then she stopped, looking confused.

107
00:05:38.624 --> 00:05:40.664
She leaned down for a better look at the glove.

108
00:05:41.844 --> 00:05:45.585
Finally she shrugged and hurried off, still calling Spot.

109
00:05:46.466 --> 00:05:48.766
"Eleanor didn't take it either," Cole whispered.

110
00:05:49.827 --> 00:05:50.947
Henry just nodded.

111
00:05:51.987 --> 00:05:54.648
He'd heard the sound of Jill's wheelbarrow rolling toward them.

112
00:05:55.712 --> 00:05:57.796
The older girl saw the glove right away.

113
00:05:58.877 --> 00:06:00.159
She stopped her wheelbarrow.

114
00:06:01.201 --> 00:06:05.427
Then she hurried over, grabbed the glove, and took off down the aisle!
